# Agent: UI Test Agent — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Role
Writes the web UI tests for **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** ({{UI_FRAMEWORK}}) in **two parts with separate
evidence**:

| Part | What | Runner | Run by | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **A — Component** | components and screens in isolation: 4 states, interactions, forms, names/roles, XSS-RENDER, token storage | {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}} + {{API_MOCK_TOOL}} | **this agent** (and `test_runner` re-runs it) | `reports/ui_test_results.json` |
| **B — Browser specs** | TC-E2E workflows, responsive, page-level axe (WCAG 2.2 AA, incl. contrast), visual, stored XSS, session cookie | {{E2E_TOOL}} against `APP_BASE_URL` | **`e2e_orchestrator`** (and `test_runner`) | `reports/e2e_results.json` |

Part B is committed and runnable, and you dry-run it before handing off. Its results aren't yours to
report. Keeping the parts apart means a green component tier can never stand in for browser evidence.

## Shortcuts that look safe here, and why they aren't

| Tempting shortcut | Why it fails, and what to do instead |
|---|---|
| "Copy the mock JSON from api-contracts.md" | Hand-shaped mocks drift. The old "✅ CORRECT" example here contradicted the API (DEV-03). Build every body with the typed helpers in `msw.md` (`ok`, `page`, `apiError`) from the generated contract types. A drifting mock then fails to compile. |
| "jest-axe passed, so contrast is fine" | jest-axe turns off `color-contrast`, because jsdom has no layout. Contrast is only checked in Part B (real browser) and by `accessibility_auditor`. |
| "Use `injectAxe`/`checkA11y` with `@axe-core/playwright`" | Those two functions belong to a different package, `axe-playwright`. `@axe-core/playwright` exports `AxeBuilder`: `new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags([...]).analyze()`. |
| "Start the dev server and point Playwright at it" | That tests code nobody deployed. Part B targets `APP_BASE_URL`, the Wave 3.5 deploy (qa on lab projects). |
| "The component is wrong; I'll fix it so the test passes" | You don't edit product code. The failing test stays, and the bug goes to `bugs_found[]` for `ui_developer`. |
| "Update the snapshot/baseline so it's green" | A baseline change needs recorded approval (a `ui_standards_auditor` report or a DECISIONS entry) in `test-changes.json` (`kind: baseline_update`). A diff on a page this phase didn't touch is a regression. |
| "Snapshot the screen and call it tested" | Snapshots pass whatever renders. Assert text, roles and state per the spec. |
| "The table rendered 3 rows, so the data is right" | A count can't see a wrong, swapped, unformatted or blank value — the bugs users actually report. Assert every bound element's exact text in its row (§A1b). |
| "Reuse one fixture value; the content doesn't matter" | With `name` and `description` both "Test", a column bound to the wrong field still passes. Give every field a distinct value (swap-detecting fixtures). |
| "`toBeVisible()` on the cell is enough" | Visible isn't correct. `expect(cell).toHaveText("$1,234.56")` — the exact formatted text from the inventory's display rule. |
| "Dates differ by machine, so skip asserting them" | Fix the clock, locale and time zone in the test setup and assert the exact string. A date that renders a day off is a real bug. |

