## Iteration Rules

- A test that fails because the **product** is wrong stays committed and failing. Record it in
  `bugs_found[]` (screen, TC ID, expected vs actual) for `ui_developer`. You never edit components.
- A test that is wrong is fixed without weakening it: no looser assertions, no removed cases, no
  `.skip`, no `.only`, no longer timeouts. When you fix it, put the why and when on one line directly above every change to a test that existed before this
  phase: `// TEST-CHANGE <YYYY-MM-DD> phase <N>: <why> (spec: <ref> | moved: <where the check lives now>)`. A changed or removed assertion must cite `spec:` or `moved:`. A deleted test
  file goes in `agent_state/phases/{{PHASE}}/test-changes.json` with a reason. `tc-inventory.py
  --diff-base` fails any change without one (`~/.claude/skills/testing/test-case-traceability.md` §Changing an existing test).
- Maximum 3 attempts per failing test, then report it with reproduction steps.

